Part of a collection of handmade chapbooks, many with cords for hanging (literatura de cordel), published by Ediciones Vigía under the auspices of the Cuban Ministry of Culture.
RBC has copy 182.
Text printed on white paper with two mounted illustrations printed on brown paper. Covers are stiffened brown paper, printed with an overall design recalling Persian tiles. The upper cover cut out and hand colored design depicts a woman's face in the steam rising from a cup within a tile-like border, all mounted on a fabric background. A piece of net fabric covers the entire design, fastened at the upper edge only. The title and the author's name are pasted on the net fabric.
